<title>FRANCE: RPR gets Euro marketing OK for Granocyte.</title>
<headline>RPR gets Euro marketing OK for Granocyte.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer said it had received European Commission marketing authorisation for Granocyte for use in peripheral blood progenitor cell (PBC) mobilisation for autologous transplantation.</p>
<p>This process is a medical procedure performed on cancer patients to avoid a bone marrow transplant and enables a physician to administer high doses of chemotherapy.</p>
<p>Rhone-Poulenc Rorer is majority-owned by Rhone-Poulenc.</p>
